Implemented all 8 list operations in `list_ops.py:1` using only loops and list concatenation (no builtins like `len`, `map`, `filter`, `sum`, `reversed`, or `sorted`):

- `append` — copies items from both lists into a new list
- `concat` — flattens a series of lists
- `filter` — keeps items where `function(item)` is truthy
- `length` — counts items
- `map` — applies `function` to each item
- `foldl` — left fold, `function(accumulator, item)`
- `foldr` — right fold via `reverse`, `function(item, accumulator)`
- `reverse` — prepends each item to build a reversed list

